if (list_entry_is_head(storage, &map->list, list_map))
Reason:
`list_entry_is_head()` correctly checks whether the pointer obtained from `list_next_entry()` is the list head (i.e., the dummy head of the list), which indicates that we have iterated past the last element. This allows the function to return `-ENOENT` when there are no more entries, preventing the bogus read.

